; Two increments of one counter.  Each firing takes the counter's row, so two
; firings cannot both read the old value: no step loses an update.  The bags
; of both members are never enabled (they would take one row twice), and every
; has no step at all, since both matches need the same row.
(inc x) (inc y)
(count z)
(rule bump (take (inc $i) (count $n)) (make (count (s $n)) (bumped $i)))
